Z||000006||Songman||08-10-2001||12:45 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PBJ:<BR><B>Nice lookin car.  I was lookin at one tonight, I did not realize that they have (or atleast the one I saw) red lined at 7500 rpm and is a 2.7L based on the 2.5L</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>If you were looking at one with a 2.7 it was not a street car, but one of the Indy track cars. As far as I know, none of those are on the street.<P>The Pace Cars for the street are nothing but 84 SEs with custom coloring. Mechanically, they are the same in every way as every other 84 Fiero.<P>My Indy is on the far left in this picture...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycars7.jpg"> <P>The T-top in the foreground will soon be an Indy clone with a little help from Aus and his cool new parts. Here's the mock up that he did for me.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AUSindypace2a.jpg"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
